-- title:
--   Index of n-th powers in local units when μₙ ⊆ Kᵥ
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, let $v$ be a point of the height-one spectrum of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_K$, and write $K_v$ for the $v$-adic completion of $K$ and $\mathcal{O}_v =$ `v.adicCompletionIntegers K` for its valuation subring. Let $n$ be a natural number and assume that the set `primitiveRoots n (v.adicCompletion K)` is nonempty, i.e. that $K_v$ contains an element which is a primitive $n$-th root of unity (this in particular forces $n > 0$). Then the cardinality, as a natural number, of the quotient of the unit group $\mathcal{O}_v^\times$ by the range of the monoid endomorphism $x \mapsto x^n$ of $\mathcal{O}_v^\times$ equals
--   $$n \cdot \#\bigl(\mathcal{O}_v / n\mathcal{O}_v\bigr),$$
--   where the second factor is the cardinality of the quotient of $\mathcal{O}_v$ by the ideal generated by the image of $n$ in $\mathcal{O}_v$. Equivalently, $[\mathcal{O}_v^\times : (\mathcal{O}_v^\times)^n] = n\,\#(\mathcal{O}_v/n\mathcal{O}_v)$. Note that the statement is about $\mathrm{Nat.card}$ of the quotient group, so it carries no separate finiteness assertion beyond the equality of cardinalities.
--
--   This is the unit-group half of the classical computation of the index of $n$-th powers in a local field containing the $n$-th roots of unity; it is used by [`NumberField.natCard_units_adicCompletion_quotient_range_powMonoidHom`](thm.html#NumberField.natCard_units_adicCompletion_quotient_range_powMonoidHom), which supplies the additional factor coming from the value group $K_v^\times/\mathcal{O}_v^\times$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_NumberField_natCard_units_adicCompletionIntegers_quotient_range_powMonoidHom.lean

